{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-32066","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43934","text":"RFC — Evidence Residency ("},{"id":"spn-43935","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-43936","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-32067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43937","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status."},{"id":"spn-43938","text":" Ruled (user, 2026-07-23). This RFC freezes the first non-TRVM TRAAVIIS environment "},{"id":"spn-43939","marks":["italic"],"text":"before any code is written"},{"id":"spn-43940","text":". It scopes exactly one task, one one-shot agent interface, and the snapshot / output / verifier / reward / replayability contracts. Nothing here requires WallRiderLang lowering or TRVM interaction-calculus reduction. Code is held until these contracts are frozen."}]},{"id":"blk-32068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43941","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-43942","text":" TRAAVIIS is an "},{"id":"spn-43943","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environment for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-43944","text":". Its value is not \"deterministic worlds\" but: "},{"id":"spn-43945","marks":["italic"],"text":"an agent's work should leave inspectable evidence that survives replay, verification, disagreement, and human review."},{"id":"spn-43946","text":" Evidence Residency is the first environment that makes that concrete for a real repository, and it is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-43947","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-43948","text":" a TRVM world."}]},{"id":"blk-32069","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43949","text":"1. Substrate ruling — TRAAVIIS is substrate-neutral"}]},{"id":"blk-32070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43950","text":"TRAAVIIS evaluates over multiple substrates. TRVM is one — uniquely strong, but no longer the definition of everything TRAAVIIS can evaluate."}]},{"id":"blk-32071","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRAAVIIS\nsubstrate-neutral evaluation and evidence layer\n        │\n        ├── TRVM substrate            (trvm.world.v1)\n        │     sem · scen · film\n        │     reference · native · oracle\n        │\n        └── Residency substrate       (residency.repository.v1)\n              snapshot · finding · patch · trace\n              citations · patch · tests · identity"},{"id":"blk-32072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43951","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-43952","text":" is an "},{"id":"spn-43953","marks":["bold"],"text":"external evidence environment orchestrated by TRAAVIIS"},{"id":"spn-43954","text":". TRAAVIIS prepares a frozen subject, runs an agent command in a controlled workspace, collects evidence, and checks it with external deterministic verifiers. It does not fold anything through "},{"id":"spn-43955","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-43956","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-43957","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-43958","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32073","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43959","text":"2. The common ladder (shared) vs substrate-specific artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-32074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43960","text":"Four constructs are "},{"id":"spn-43961","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-43962","text":" across every substrate:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32076","spans":[{"id":"spn-43963","text":"construct"}]},{"id":"blk-32077","spans":[{"id":"spn-43964","text":"question it answers"}]}],"id":"blk-32075","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32078","spans":[{"id":"spn-43965","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-32079","spans":[{"id":"spn-43966","text":"what must be done?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32080","spans":[{"id":"spn-43967","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-32081","spans":[{"id":"spn-43968","text":"how is admissible evidence scored?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32082","spans":[{"id":"spn-43969","marks":["code"],"text":"SubstrateProfileV1"}]},{"id":"blk-32083","spans":[{"id":"spn-43970","text":"how is the subject prepared and evidence collected?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32084","spans":[{"id":"spn-43971","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1"}]},{"id":"blk-32085","spans":[{"id":"spn-43972","text":"what happened, what was produced, what passed, what score?"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32086","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43973","text":"Substrate-specific evidence lives "},{"id":"spn-43974","marks":["bold"],"text":"below"},{"id":"spn-43975","text":" the shared ladder:"}]},{"id":"blk-32087","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRVM       sem · scen · film\nResidency  snap · trace · finding · patch"},{"id":"blk-32088","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43976","text":"2a. Correction — "},{"id":"spn-43977","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-43978","text":" is TRVM-only; the neutral trace is "},{"id":"spn-43979","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-32089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-43980","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-43981","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…` is a TRVM deterministic-execution artifact"},{"id":"spn-43982","text":" and stays that way. It does "},{"id":"spn-43983","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-43984","text":" generalize to arbitrary substrates. The substrate-neutral observable record is a "},{"id":"spn-43985","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-43986","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-43987","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-43988","text":" object is the "},{"id":"spn-43989","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode-…`"},{"id":"spn-43990","text":" receipt, which references whichever substrate-specific evidence exists plus a "},{"id":"spn-43991","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile"},{"id":"spn-43992","text":". We do not pretend the underlying execution mechanisms are identical."}]},{"id":"blk-32090","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-43993","text":"3. Three meanings of \"replay\" (freeze this distinction)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32092","spans":[{"id":"spn-43994","text":"level"}]},{"id":"blk-32093","spans":[{"id":"spn-43995","text":"meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-32094","spans":[{"id":"spn-43996","text":"who supports it"}]}],"id":"blk-32091","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32095","spans":[{"id":"spn-43997","marks":["bold"],"text":"exact replay"}]},{"id":"blk-32096","spans":[{"id":"spn-43998","text":"re-running canonical inputs reproduces the same state trajectory and film"}]},{"id":"blk-32097","spans":[{"id":"spn-43999","text":"TRVM"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32098","spans":[{"id":"spn-44000","marks":["bold"],"text":"action replay"}]},{"id":"blk-32099","spans":[{"id":"spn-44001","text":"recorded tool calls are reapplied against the same frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-32100","spans":[{"id":"spn-44002","text":"a controlled Residency runner, "},{"id":"spn-44003","marks":["italic"],"text":"later"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32101","spans":[{"id":"spn-44004","marks":["bold"],"text":"verification replay"}]},{"id":"blk-32102","spans":[{"id":"spn-44005","text":"the submitted finding, patch and receipts are re-checked against the frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-32103","spans":[{"id":"spn-44006","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32104","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44007","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1 promises only verification replay."},{"id":"spn-44008","text":" We do "},{"id":"spn-44009","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-44010","text":" promise deterministic replay of an arbitrary external coding-agent process — shell tools, package registries, clocks, and OS behaviour make that a much larger claim. Residency v1 honestly promises:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44011","text":"The evidence and outcome can be independently reverified."}]}],"id":"blk-32105","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-32107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44012","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1.replayability"},{"id":"spn-44013","text":" records which level applies ("},{"id":"spn-44014","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-44015","text":" for TRVM, "},{"id":"spn-44016","marks":["code"],"text":"verification"},{"id":"spn-44017","text":" for Residency v1)."}]},{"id":"blk-32108","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44018","text":"4. Frozen subject — "},{"id":"spn-44019","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1"},{"id":"spn-44020","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-44021","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]},{"id":"blk-32109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44022","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44023","text":" seals "},{"id":"spn-44024","marks":["bold"],"text":"only the subject"},{"id":"spn-44025","text":" — the repository the agent sees — "},{"id":"spn-44026","marks":["bold"],"text":"not the evaluation procedure"},{"id":"spn-44027","text":". The same frozen repository must remain the same "},{"id":"spn-44028","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44029","text":" even when evaluated under a different test plan."}]},{"id":"blk-32110","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"snapshot_version\": \"residency.snapshot.v1\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"snap-…\",\n  \"files\": { \"<relpath>\": \"<content-hash>\", … },\n  \"exclusions\": [ \"<glob>\", … ],\n  \"file_modes\": { \"<relpath>\": \"0755\", … },\n  \"base_revision\": \"<vcs-rev or null>\",\n  \"visible_config\": { … } }"},{"id":"blk-32111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44030","text":"Seal: repository bytes, normalized relative paths, file modes, exclusions, base revision if available, task-visible repository config. "},{"id":"spn-44031","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not seal"},{"id":"spn-44032","text":" timestamps or absolute machine paths — they would make the snapshot machine-specific without changing its meaning. "},{"id":"spn-44033","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44034","text":" is a content hash of the canonical sealed bytes."}]},{"id":"blk-32112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44035","marks":["bold"],"text":"Ownership split (erratum)."},{"id":"spn-44036","text":" The evaluation procedure lives in "},{"id":"spn-44037","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-44038","text":", not the snapshot:"}]},{"id":"blk-32113","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32115","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44039","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SnapshotV1`"},{"id":"spn-44040","text":" seals — repository bytes, relative paths, file modes,"}]}],"id":"blk-32114","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44041","text":"exclusions, base revision, task-visible repository config."}]},{"id":"blk-32117","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32119","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44042","marks":["bold"],"text":"`TaskSpecV1`"},{"id":"spn-44043","text":" seals — declared test commands, required toolchain"}]}],"id":"blk-32118","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44044","text":"constraints, the verifier plan, and the agent execution policy (§7)."}]},{"id":"blk-32121","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32123","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44045","marks":["bold"],"text":"`EpisodeReceiptV1`"},{"id":"spn-44046","text":" records — "},{"id":"spn-44047","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-44048","text":" toolchain versions, "},{"id":"spn-44049","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-44050","text":" verifier"}]}],"id":"blk-32122","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44051","text":"versions, command exit codes, and platform facts relevant to verification."}]},{"id":"blk-32125","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44052","text":"This yields the right mutation behaviour:"}]},{"id":"blk-32126","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository bytes   → snap / task / episode may move\nchange test command       → task / episode move ; snap unchanged\nrun on a different actual toolchain → episode moves ; task and snap stable"},{"id":"blk-32127","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44053","text":"5. Agent outputs — "},{"id":"spn-44054","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-44055","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44056","marks":["code"],"text":"PatchV1"},{"id":"spn-44057","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44058","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"}]},{"id":"blk-32128","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"FindingV1 → finding-…    structured claims + citations (not only prose)\nPatchV1   → patch-…      a unified diff that applies to a clean snapshot copy\nTraceV1   → trace-…      substrate-neutral record of observable process events"},{"id":"blk-32129","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44059","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-44060","text":" must carry "},{"id":"spn-44061","marks":["bold"],"text":"structured"},{"id":"spn-44062","text":" claims and citations, each citation resolving to exact supporting material inside the snapshot. Spans are "},{"id":"spn-44063","marks":["bold"],"text":"1-based inclusive line ranges"},{"id":"spn-44064","text":" expressed as an explicit object (never an ambiguous two-element array), and the "},{"id":"spn-44065","marks":["code"],"text":"quote"},{"id":"spn-44066","text":" must match the normalized snapshot bytes exactly:"}]},{"id":"blk-32130","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"finding_version\": \"residency.finding.v1\",\n  \"finding_id\": \"finding-…\",\n  \"claims\": [ { \"statement\": \"…\",\n                \"citations\": [ { \"path\": \"spec/WRL_CORE_0.1.md\",\n                                 \"start_line\": 120, \"end_line\": 138,\n                                 \"quote\": \"…\" } ] } ] }"},{"id":"blk-32131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44067","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"},{"id":"spn-44068","text":" records observable events — enough to review and to drive "},{"id":"spn-44069","marks":["italic"],"text":"action replay"},{"id":"spn-44070","text":" later, without claiming determinism now."}]},{"id":"blk-32132","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44071","text":"5a. Canonical evidence rules (freeze before generating any IDs)"}]},{"id":"blk-32133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44072","marks":["bold"],"text":"Snapshot paths."},{"id":"spn-44073","text":" UTF-8 relative POSIX paths; no absolute paths; no "},{"id":"spn-44074","marks":["code"],"text":".."},{"id":"spn-44075","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-44076","marks":["code"],"text":"/"},{"id":"spn-44077","text":" separator on every platform; explicit symlink policy (v1: symlinks excluded); explicit line-ending policy (v1: normalize to LF for text, byte-exact for declared-binary)."}]},{"id":"blk-32134","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44078","marks":["bold"],"text":"Citations."},{"id":"spn-44079","text":" 1-based inclusive line ranges as "},{"id":"spn-44080","marks":["code"],"text":"{start_line, end_line}"},{"id":"spn-44081","text":"; the quoted text matches the normalized snapshot bytes exactly."}]},{"id":"blk-32135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44082","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patches."},{"id":"spn-44083","text":" Unified diff; relative paths only; no timestamps; fixed "},{"id":"spn-44084","marks":["code"],"text":"a/"},{"id":"spn-44085","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-44086","marks":["code"],"text":"b/"},{"id":"spn-44087","text":" prefixes; LF line endings; "},{"id":"spn-44088","marks":["bold"],"text":"no binary patches in v1"},{"id":"spn-44089","text":"; canonical file ordering (sorted by POSIX path)."}]},{"id":"blk-32136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44090","marks":["bold"],"text":"Traces."},{"id":"spn-44091","text":" Exclude volatile timestamps and host paths from "},{"id":"spn-44092","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-44093","text":" identity. The canonical trace records deterministic events only:"}]},{"id":"blk-32137","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"command argv · relative cwd · declared environment keys · exit code\nstdout digest · stderr digest · files-created digest · files-modified digest\nresult-file digest"},{"id":"blk-32138","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44094","text":"Human-readable timed logs may exist beside the canonical trace "},{"id":"spn-44095","marks":["bold"],"text":"without"},{"id":"spn-44096","text":" entering its identity."}]},{"id":"blk-32139","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44097","text":"6. Verifier applicability — four states"}]},{"id":"blk-32140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44098","text":"Every verifier returns exactly one of:"}]},{"id":"blk-32141","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pass · fail · not_applicable · error"},{"id":"blk-32142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44099","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44100","text":" "},{"id":"spn-44101","marks":["bold"],"text":"must remain distinct"},{"id":"spn-44102","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-44103","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44104","text":": an unavailable test runner is not evidence that the candidate patch is wrong. "},{"id":"spn-44105","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-44106","text":" is coverage honesty (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-44107","marks":["code"],"text":"native"},{"id":"spn-44108","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-44109","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"},{"id":"spn-44110","text":" on a Residency episode). The receipt's verification map is "},{"id":"spn-44111","marks":["bold"],"text":"total"},{"id":"spn-44112","text":" — every declared verifier reports one of the four."}]},{"id":"blk-32143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44113","text":"Residency v1 verifier set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32145","spans":[{"id":"spn-44114","text":"verifier"}]},{"id":"blk-32146","spans":[{"id":"spn-44115","text":"checks"}]}],"id":"blk-32144","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32147","spans":[{"id":"spn-44116","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"}]},{"id":"blk-32148","spans":[{"id":"spn-44117","text":"every finding citation resolves and the quote matches source"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32149","spans":[{"id":"spn-44118","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"}]},{"id":"blk-32150","spans":[{"id":"spn-44119","text":"the patch applies cleanly to a fresh copy of "},{"id":"spn-44120","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32151","spans":[{"id":"spn-44121","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"}]},{"id":"blk-32152","spans":[{"id":"spn-44122","text":"the declared "},{"id":"spn-44123","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-44124","text":" pass on the patched copy"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32153","spans":[{"id":"spn-44125","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"}]},{"id":"blk-32154","spans":[{"id":"spn-44126","text":"semantic identity moved only within allowed domains"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32155","spans":[{"id":"spn-44127","marks":["code"],"text":"native"}]},{"id":"blk-32156","spans":[{"id":"spn-44128","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-44129","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32157","spans":[{"id":"spn-44130","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"}]},{"id":"blk-32158","spans":[{"id":"spn-44131","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-44132","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32159","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44133","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-44134","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-44135","text":" verifier is where TRVM's guarantees re-enter: if the task touches a WRL world, the frozen "},{"id":"spn-44136","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-44137","text":" domains that must not move are checked with the existing Forge re-lower — a Residency episode can "},{"id":"spn-44138","marks":["italic"],"text":"depend on"},{"id":"spn-44139","text":" a TRVM identity check without "},{"id":"spn-44140","marks":["italic"],"text":"being"},{"id":"spn-44141","text":" a TRVM fold."}]},{"id":"blk-32160","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44142","text":"6a. Verifier state → reward behavior (frozen)"}]},{"id":"blk-32161","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44143","text":"The four verifier states map to reward behavior by a fixed table. "},{"id":"spn-44144","marks":["bold"],"text":"A test runner failure is not evidence that the agent's work was incorrect"},{"id":"spn-44145","text":" — it is substrate unavailability, and it must never be scored as a "},{"id":"spn-44146","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44147","text":"."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-32163","spans":[{"id":"spn-44148","text":"State"}]},{"id":"blk-32164","spans":[{"id":"spn-44149","text":"Reward behavior"}]}],"id":"blk-32162","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-32165","spans":[{"id":"spn-44150","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"}]},{"id":"blk-32166","spans":[{"id":"spn-44151","text":"signal receives its positive value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32167","spans":[{"id":"spn-44152","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"}]},{"id":"blk-32168","spans":[{"id":"spn-44153","text":"signal receives zero; applicable floors/caps run"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32169","spans":[{"id":"spn-44154","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-32170","spans":[{"id":"spn-44155","text":"allowed only when the task declares the signal non-required"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32171","spans":[{"id":"spn-44156","marks":["code"],"text":"error"}]},{"id":"blk-32172","spans":[{"id":"spn-44157","text":"episode "},{"id":"spn-44158","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-44159","text":" becomes "},{"id":"spn-44160","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44161","text":"; reward is "},{"id":"spn-44162","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-44163","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-44164","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32173","spans":[{"id":"spn-44165","text":"required verifier returns "},{"id":"spn-44166","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-32174","spans":[{"id":"spn-44167","text":"invalid task configuration ("},{"id":"spn-44168","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-44169","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-32175","spans":[{"id":"spn-44170","text":"snapshot tampering"}]},{"id":"blk-32176","spans":[{"id":"spn-44171","text":"invalid episode ("},{"id":"spn-44172","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-44173","text":"); reward "},{"id":"spn-44174","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-32177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44175","text":"The distinction between "},{"id":"spn-44176","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-44177","text":" (an "},{"id":"spn-44178","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44179","text":" episode: scoring could not be computed) and "},{"id":"spn-44180","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-44181","text":" (a real "},{"id":"spn-44182","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44183","text":" or a tamper) is load-bearing. Downstream aggregation must drop "},{"id":"spn-44184","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-44185","text":"-reward episodes, never average them in as zeros."}]},{"id":"blk-32178","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44186","text":"7. Reward — deterministic, decomposable, no LLM prose judging"}]},{"id":"blk-32179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44187","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-44188","text":" for the first task is a "},{"id":"spn-44189","marks":["bold"],"text":"canonical keyed signal map"},{"id":"spn-44190","text":" (see "},{"id":"spn-44191","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"},{"id":"spn-44192","text":" §2): each key binds one verifier result to one weight. The identifiers are load-bearing — renaming a signal moves "},{"id":"spn-44193","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-44194","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32180","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"citations             → residency.citations.v1   0.25\npatch                 → residency.patch.v1        0.20\ntests                 → residency.tests.v1        0.30\nidentity              → residency.identity.v1     0.15\nfinding_completeness  → residency.finding.v1      0.10"},{"id":"blk-32181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44195","marks":["bold"],"text":"`finding completeness` means required structured fields + evidence coverage"},{"id":"spn-44196","text":", never prose quality judged by another model. No signal in Residency v1 calls an LLM; every signal is a pure function over sealed evidence."}]},{"id":"blk-32182","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44197","marks":["bold"],"text":"Hard floors (caps, applied after the weighted sum):"}]},{"id":"blk-32183","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"patch does not apply        → reward ≤ 0.25\ncitations do not resolve    → reward ≤ 0.25\nrequired tests regress      → reward ≤ 0.40\ntampered snapshot           → reward = 0 and episode marked invalid"},{"id":"blk-32184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44198","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-44199","text":" is the content hash of the canonical "},{"id":"spn-44200","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-44201","text":" (weights + floors + verifier binding)."}]},{"id":"blk-32185","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44202","text":"8. First task (one, narrow, bounded)"}]},{"id":"blk-32186","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"task: residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001\n\nIdentify one real inconsistency between a frozen WallRiderLang specification and\nits implementation. Cite the exact conflicting evidence, propose the smallest\npatch, run the declared acceptance checks, and preserve identities that should\nnot move."},{"id":"blk-32187","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44203","text":"Bounded corpus, explicit success contract. The agent is "},{"id":"spn-44204","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-44205","text":" asked to search for any possible improvement — it is given a fixed snapshot and a single, checkable objective."}]},{"id":"blk-32188","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44206","text":"9. Mutation laws (freeze; test-first before code)"}]},{"id":"blk-32189","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository input\n  → snap / task / trace / finding / patch / episode may move\n\nchange task instructions\n  → task / episode move\n  → snap unchanged\n\nchange reward weights\n  → rew / episode move\n  → snap / trace / finding / patch unchanged\n\nchange agent output\n  → finding / patch / trace / episode move\n  → task / snap unchanged\n\nrerun the SAME verifier versions over identical frozen artifacts\n  UNDER identical canonical execution facts\n  → episode identity remains stable\n\nchange verifier implementation version\n  OR change canonical execution facts (toolchain, exit codes, platform)\n  → episode moves\n  → underlying evidence artifacts (snap / trace / finding / patch) unchanged"},{"id":"blk-32190","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44207","text":"The stability law is stated precisely because the receipt records "},{"id":"spn-44208","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-44209","text":". Stability holds only when "},{"id":"spn-44210","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-44211","text":" the verifier versions "},{"id":"spn-44212","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-44213","text":" the "},{"id":"spn-44214","marks":["italic"],"text":"canonical"},{"id":"spn-44215","text":" execution facts are identical; changing either moves the "},{"id":"spn-44216","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-44217","text":". (The "},{"id":"spn-44218","marks":["italic"],"text":"volatile"},{"id":"spn-44219","text":" execution facts — wall-clock, absolute paths, transient PIDs — are excluded from the hash, so they never move it.) This reconciles with the already-stated law that a different "},{"id":"spn-44220","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-44221","text":" toolchain moves the episode: "},{"id":"spn-44222","marks":["bold"],"text":"verifier versions and canonical execution facts are recorded in the receipt"},{"id":"spn-44223","text":", so a scoring-logic change or a toolchain change is auditable and moves the "},{"id":"spn-44224","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-44225","text":" without rewriting what the agent actually produced."}]},{"id":"blk-32191","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44226","text":"10. "},{"id":"spn-44227","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-44228","text":" — the one-shot interface (first implementation)"}]},{"id":"blk-32192","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"trvs eval-one residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001.json \\\n  --agent-command \"./stub-agent\""},{"id":"blk-32193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44229","text":"The agent command receives a frozen workspace and emits one structured final result:"}]},{"id":"blk-32194","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"format\": \"traaviis.agent-result.v1\",\n  \"finding\": { \"summary\": \"…\", \"citations\": [ … ] },\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-32195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44230","text":"TRAAVIIS then, independently and deterministically:"}]},{"id":"blk-32196","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32198","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44231","text":"snapshots the starting repository → "},{"id":"spn-44232","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44233","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32197","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44234","text":"runs the command in a controlled workspace;"}]}],"id":"blk-32199","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44235","text":"captures observable process events → "},{"id":"spn-44236","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-44237","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32201","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44238","text":"reads the proposed finding and patch → "},{"id":"spn-44239","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-44240","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44241","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-44242","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32203","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32206","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44243","text":"resolves citations against "},{"id":"spn-44244","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44245","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32205","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44246","text":"applies the patch to a clean copy of "},{"id":"spn-44247","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44248","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32207","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44249","text":"runs the declared "},{"id":"spn-44250","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-44251","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-32209","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44252","text":"measures identity movement;"}]}],"id":"blk-32211","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44253","text":"calculates the reward (weights + floors);"}]}],"id":"blk-32213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44254","text":"emits "},{"id":"spn-44255","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-44256","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-32215","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-32217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44257","text":"A richer interactive N-step action protocol (and the ORS adapter over the Episode Kernel) can follow "},{"id":"spn-44258","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-44259","text":" this one-shot path works and is boring."}]},{"id":"blk-32218","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44260","text":"10a. "},{"id":"spn-44261","marks":["code"],"text":"AgentRunPolicyV1"},{"id":"spn-44262","text":" — the frozen one-shot execution policy"}]},{"id":"blk-32219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44263","text":"The task carries an "},{"id":"spn-44264","marks":["code"],"text":"agent_run_policy"},{"id":"spn-44265","text":" sub-document. It is part of the "},{"id":"spn-44266","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-44267","text":" identity: changing how the agent is allowed to run changes "},{"id":"spn-44268","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-44269","text":". The runner enforces it; the receipt records what actually happened."}]},{"id":"blk-32220","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"policy_version\": \"traaviis.agent-run-policy.v1\",\n  \"command_mode\": \"argv\",\n  \"shell\": false,\n  \"network\": \"disabled\",\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 900,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 4194304,\n  \"environment\": { \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\", \"HOME\": \"/sandbox/home\" },\n  \"toolchain_profile\": \"residency.python-3.11.v1\",\n  \"writable_paths\": [\".\"],\n  \"result_path\": \"result.json\",\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-32221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44270","text":"Rules:"}]},{"id":"blk-32222","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44271","marks":["bold"],"text":"`command_mode: argv`, `shell: false`"},{"id":"spn-44272","text":" — the agent command is an argv vector"}]}],"id":"blk-32223","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44273","text":"executed without a shell. No shell interpolation is part of the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-32226","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44274","marks":["bold"],"text":"`network: disabled`"},{"id":"spn-44275","text":" by default — a task that needs the network must declare"}]}],"id":"blk-32227","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32229","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44276","text":"it explicitly, and that declaration moves "},{"id":"spn-44277","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-44278","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32230","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44279","marks":["bold"],"text":"`timeout_seconds` / `max_output_bytes`"},{"id":"spn-44280","text":" are hard bounds. Exceeding either"}]}],"id":"blk-32231","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44281","text":"terminates the run; the episode records the termination reason and the affected verifier reports "},{"id":"spn-44282","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44283","text":" (substrate unavailability), not "},{"id":"spn-44284","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44285","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32234","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44286","marks":["bold"],"text":"`environment` is a sealed key→value map, not a host allowlist."},{"id":"spn-44287","text":" Host"}]}],"id":"blk-32235","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44288","text":"environment values ("},{"id":"spn-44289","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-44290","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44291","marks":["code"],"text":"HOME"},{"id":"spn-44292","text":", "},{"id":"spn-44293","marks":["code"],"text":"LANG"},{"id":"spn-44294","text":", …) are "},{"id":"spn-44295","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-44296","text":" inherited — their values could change behavior without entering "},{"id":"spn-44297","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-44298","text":", which would break the frozen-subject claim. Only the sealed keys with their "},{"id":"spn-44299","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed, normalized values"},{"id":"spn-44300","text":" are exported; everything else is stripped. The runner constructs a controlled "},{"id":"spn-44301","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-44302","text":" from the "},{"id":"spn-44303","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-44304","text":"; it never inherits the host's arbitrary "},{"id":"spn-44305","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-44306","text":". An allowlist is safe only when "},{"id":"spn-44307","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-44308","text":" the key "},{"id":"spn-44309","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-44310","text":" its normalized value are fixed, which is exactly what a sealed map is."}]},{"id":"blk-32238","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44311","marks":["bold"],"text":"`toolchain_profile`"},{"id":"spn-44312","text":" names the sealed toolchain (interpreter, package set)."}]}],"id":"blk-32239","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44313","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-44314","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual resolved executables and versions"},{"id":"spn-44315","text":" go into the receipt's "},{"id":"spn-44316","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-44317","text":", so a toolchain drift is auditable and moves "},{"id":"spn-44318","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-44319","text":" (see §9), while the "},{"id":"spn-44320","marks":["italic"],"text":"declared"},{"id":"spn-44321","text":" profile is part of "},{"id":"spn-44322","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-44323","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32242","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44324","marks":["bold"],"text":"`writable_paths`"},{"id":"spn-44325","text":" scopes filesystem mutation; writes outside the set are a"}]}],"id":"blk-32243","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32245","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44326","text":"policy violation that invalidates the episode."}]},{"id":"blk-32246","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44327","marks":["bold"],"text":"`result_path` / `patch_path`"},{"id":"spn-44328","text":" are where the runner reads the structured"}]}],"id":"blk-32247","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44329","text":"result and the candidate patch after the process exits. Absence of a required output is a "},{"id":"spn-44330","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44331","text":" for the corresponding verifier, never an "},{"id":"spn-44332","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44333","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32250","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44334","text":"The distinction is deliberate: a "},{"id":"spn-44335","marks":["bold"],"text":"policy or substrate failure"},{"id":"spn-44336","text":" (timeout, output cap, missing runner) yields "},{"id":"spn-44337","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44338","text":"; a "},{"id":"spn-44339","marks":["bold"],"text":"missing or malformed agent output"},{"id":"spn-44340","text":" yields "},{"id":"spn-44341","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-44342","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32251","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44343","text":"11. Example receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-32252","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44344","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM episode"},{"id":"spn-44345","text":" (Golden Spinner, unchanged):"}]},{"id":"blk-32253","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"film-…\",\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"pass\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"reference\": \"1\", \"native\": \"1\", \"oracle\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"exact\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"reducer\": \"ic32\", \"epochs\": 9 } }"},{"id":"blk-32254","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44346","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-32255","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"snapshot\": \"snap-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"trace-…\",\n  \"outputs\": { \"finding\": \"finding-…\", \"patch\": \"patch-…\" },\n  \"verification\": { \"citations\": \"pass\", \"patch\": \"pass\", \"tests\": \"pass\",\n                    \"identity\": \"pass\",\n                    \"native\": \"not_applicable\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"citations\": \"1\", \"patch\": \"1\", \"tests\": \"1\", \"identity\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1.0,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"verification\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"exit_code\": 0, \"platform\": \"linux-x86_64\",\n                       \"timed_out\": false, \"output_truncated\": false } }"},{"id":"blk-32256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44347","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-44348","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-44349","marks":["code"],"text":"ok | error | invalid"},{"id":"spn-44350","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-44351","marks":["code"],"text":"validity"},{"id":"spn-44352","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-44353","marks":["code"],"text":"valid | invalid"},{"id":"spn-44354","text":". An "},{"id":"spn-44355","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-44356","text":" episode carries "},{"id":"spn-44357","marks":["code"],"text":"reward: null"},{"id":"spn-44358","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-32257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44359","text":"Canonical "},{"id":"spn-44360","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-44361","text":" — including resolved toolchain versions, normalized platform, exit codes, timeout state, and output-truncation state — enter the "},{"id":"spn-44362","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_id"},{"id":"spn-44363","text":" hash. Volatile execution metadata — wall-clock timestamps, absolute paths, transient process IDs, and host-specific log locations — is excluded."}]},{"id":"blk-32258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44364","text":"Same ladder, honest about different execution mechanisms."}]},{"id":"blk-32259","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-44365","text":"12. Held until this RFC is accepted"}]},{"id":"blk-32260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44366","text":"Not built now: the interactive N-step environment protocol, ORS/MCP adapters, batch "},{"id":"spn-44367","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-44368","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-44369","marks":["code"],"text":"compare"},{"id":"spn-44370","text":", action replay, a second Residency task, process rewards, and any new identity category beyond "},{"id":"spn-44371","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-44372","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-44373","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-44374","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-44375","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-44376","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-44377","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-44378","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-44379","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-44380","text":". Spinner Bench v0.7-5 proceeds independently and is not a blocker for this RFC."}]},{"id":"blk-32261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-44381","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierabejm2iluwgfud6sthvn6frov2yaqgh3invb2onfbzqv4yo55dtfq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}